  "problem": {
    "id": "train-3225",
    "question": "Chris bought 8 movies on DVD for $12 each and 4 movies on Blu-ray for $18 each. What is the average price he paid per movie?",
    "gold": "14",
    "answer": "He spent a total of 8 * $12 + 4 * $18 = $<<8*12+4*18=168>>168\nHe bought a total of 8 + 4 = <<8+4=12>>12 movies.\nThe average price is $168 / 12 = $<<168/12=14>>14 per movie.\n#### 14"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To find the average price Chris paid per movie, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total cost of the DVDs.\n2. Calculate the total cost of the Blu-rays.\n3. Find the total number of movies.\n4. Calculate the total cost of all the movies.\n5. Divide the total cost by the total number of movies to find the average price per movie.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. The cost of the DVDs is calculated as follows:\n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ DVDs} \\times \\$12 \\text{ per DVD} = \\$96\n   \\]\n\n2. The cost of the Blu-rays is calculated as follows:\n   \\[\n   4 \\text{ Blu-rays} \\times \\$18 \\text{ per Blu-ray} = \\$72\n   \\]\n\n3. The total number of movies is:\n   \\[\n   8 \\text{ DVDs} + 4 \\text{ Blu-rays} = 12 \\text{ movies}\n   \\]\n\n4. The total cost of all the movies is:\n   \\[\n   \\$96 + \\$72 = \\$168\n   \\]\n\n5. The average price per movie is calculated by dividing the total cost by the total number of movies:\n   \\[\n   \\frac{\\$168}{12 \\text{ movies}} = \\$14 \\text{ per movie}\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the average price Chris paid per movie is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
